  "term": "counterproductive work behavior",
  "definition": "Counterproductive work behavior is deliberate employee behavior at work that is unethical, illegal, or otherwise unwanted and that harms the organization. It can waste organizational resources, damage trust and the work climate, and negatively affect both organizational functioning and employee well-being.",
